= Abstract

Beams of fire sweep through my head, thrusts of pain increasingly engaged. Sensory receptors succumb, I'm
no-one now, only agony. My crimson liquid so frantically spilled. The ruby fluid of life unleashed. Ripples
ascend to the surface of my eyes, their red pens drawing at random, at will. A myriad pains begotten, in their
wake; the bastard spawn of a mutinous self. The regurgitation of my micro nemesis. Salivating red at the
prospect of my ruin, my doom. Malfunction, the means for its ascent. Bloodletting the stringent voice to
beckon my soul. So futile, any resisting tension; as death-induced mechanics propel its growth The implement,
the device of my extinction. The terminating clockwork of my gleeful bane. The definitive scourge of its
mockery. The end-art instruments lethality attained "Heed," it commands. "Heed my will". "Bleed," it says.
"Bleed you will". Falling into the clarity of undoing, scornful gods haggle for my soul Mind's eye flickers
and vellicates as I let go, taunting whispers accompany my deletion A sneering grin, the voice of my reaper.
Chanting softly the song of depletion.
